od(x) = φd(φ(x)). (4)
The encoding and decoding paths above are used to obtain a direct mapping from a hazy image to a haze-free image. As described above, a hazy image can be described as x = yˆ∗ Lr according to Retinex theory. Therefore, a dehazed image can be obtained by yˆ = x ∗ Lr−1 = x ∗ Lir, where the inverted
residual illumination map Lir = Lr−1 (For convenience, Lir is hereinafter also referred to as the illumination map). The second decoding function φr(·) based on the Retinex model is
